WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.070
3 June 2018: Fuego, in Guatemala, erupts,

2
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.750
with a column 16 to 19 kilometres high.

3
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:14.130
On its flank, the private golf resort
of La Reunión evacuated successfully.

4
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.670
About two kilometres further on, much of
the village of San Miguel Los Lotes was

5
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.070
buried, with extensive loss of life.

6
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.570
Was the resort further from the volcano?

7
00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:25.670
Pure luck?

8
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.030
Why did one place escape?

9
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.870
In this mission, you'll compare
Fuego, above a subduction zone,

10
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.230
with Iceland's Reykjanes
Peninsula, on a rift.

11
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.490
Then you'll follow Grindavík, where
fissure lava burned three homes in January

12
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.190
2024.

13
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.870
Your mission: explain why two
places, so close together,

14
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.070
had such different outcomes.
